    <value>Pauses when you take your AirPods out and resumes when you put them back. This is an estimate from nearby signals, so it can be slow or miss changes, especially on AirPods with the H2 chip. Off by default. It works together with "Pause media when AirPods are removed" in Sound, and only when the signal is probably your AirPods.</value>
    <comment>Explanation text under a control in Settings &gt; AirPods. Wraps over several lines; about 2 to 4 lines at ~480 px wide. Contains the quoted name of another setting, 'Pause media when AirPods are removed': keep it identical to SettingsPauseOnRemovalToggle.Header. 'H2' is a chip name, keep as is.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="SettingsEarDetectionUnverifiedNote.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Nearby readings can't be verified, so someone else's AirPods, or a fake signal, could trigger these.</value>
    <comment>Explanation text under a control in Settings &gt; AirPods. Wraps over several lines; about 2 to 4 lines at ~480 px wide. Same sentence as the one under Connect automatically.</comment>
  </data>
